    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-%28Architecture-and-Sustainable-Design%29-Design-Computation-138682/51149944/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design)",
      "description": "Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design) - Design Computation Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design) - Design Computation Job Req ID: 2315 Employee Category: Faculty Department: ASD Pillar Position Description The pillar of Architecture and Sustainable Design at the Singapore University of Technology and Design invites applications for a full-time Tenure-Track Assistant Professor position in Design Computation . Candidates are expected to teach an undergraduate introductory subject on design computing, graduate design studio and develop their own research-oriented elective cross-listed for both undergraduate and graduate students. Additionally, candidates are expected to conduct research and produce creative work within a research-intensive university setting, seek for research funding from relevant government and industry sources and contribute to architectural computing research via academic publishing and creative work. Job Requirement Candidates should possess an accredited graduate degree in Architecture and demonstrate outstanding past academic research, teaching and professional work in design. Applicants should submit the following documents: Cover letter Up-to-date curriculum vitae Research statement Teaching statement Recent research publications Contact information of at least three references. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-Tenure-Track-Position-in-Psychological-Sciences-%28HASS%29-138682/58460944/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track Position in Psychological Sciences (HASS)",
      "description": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track Position in Psychological Sciences (HASS) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member - Tenure-Track Position in Psychological Sciences (HASS) Job Req ID: 2553 Employee Category: Faculty Department: HASS Faculty Member - Tenure-track Position in Psychological Sciences The Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (HASS) Cluster at the Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) invites applications for an open-rank, tenure-track faculty position. We seek applicants with a scholarly background in any area of the psychological sciences. We encourage applications from candidates who can contribute productively to the Design and Artificial Intelligence (DAI) programme, in particular to our Human-centred Intelligence (HI) Track. The HI track offers instruction across fields like psychology, philosophy, and human–AI interaction, and is embedded within the broader DAI theme of leveraging human-centred design and AI methods for real-world impact. We thus seek scholars with expertise that can bridge the understanding of machine and human intelligence, and who are actively engaged in rigorous quantitative research involving both. Examples include the psychological study of human–AI interaction or the use of AI for the study of human cognition and behaviour. Candidates should have a proven record of effective teaching at the university level. An ability to teach advanced methods in statistical or computational modelling will be viewed favourably. The selected candidate will: Maintain a strong research profile including publications and grant funding. Contribute to interdisciplinary research within SUTD through collaboration with colleagues in engineering, computer science, architecture, and design. Strengthen teaching for the Design and Artificial Intelligence (DAI) undergraduate programme as well as the Psychology & Business Management Minor. Contribute to the innovation of pedagogical approaches that leverage and embody Design.AI, as well as initiatives that bridge scholarly instruction with real-world problem solving. Actively contribute to the shaping of HASS and DAI, as well as their interface with the broader SUTD ecosystem and with partners in industry and the public sector. Application Details Candidates should submit the following materials: A cover letter A curriculum vitae A statement of current and future research A statement of teaching experience and philosophy A 500-word description and selected bibliography of up to ten readings for each of two courses you may wish to offer PDF copies of two representative scholarly publications Names, affiliations, and email addresses of three referees. (Please note that candidates who advance to the interview stage will be asked to submit two letters of recommendation. Please have your recommenders ready to send their letters via email or Interfolio.) Full consideration will be given to applications received by 31 October 2026 . For more information about the position, please contact hassjobs@sutd.edu.sg . About SUTD and HASS SUTD is a young and distinctive university with a mission to nurture technically grounded leaders and innovators. Today, SUTD's Design.AI vision means that artificial intelligence is not merely a tool but a partner in the design process; together, design and AI form the backbone of our curriculum and research. The university champions cohort-based learning and interdisciplinary pedagogy, offering degrees in Architecture and Sustainable Design (ASD), Design and Artificial Intelligence (DAI), Engineering Product Development (EPD), Engineering Systems and Design (ESD), and Information Systems Technology and Design (ISTD). The Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (HASS) Cluster plays a pivotal role in the university’s commitment to world-class teaching and research excellence by providing the human-centred vision to achieve a better world by design. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-Tenure-Track-%28Engineering-Product-Development%29-138682/58462044/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track (Engineering Product Development)",
      "description": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track (Engineering Product Development) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member - Tenure-Track (Engineering Product Development) Job Req ID: 2554 Employee Category: Faculty Department: EPD Pillar The Engineering Product Development (EPD) Pillar at the Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the area of Human-Centric Embodied AI, Physical Intelligence, and World Models. As generative AI moves from digital environments into the physical world, EPD seeks an exceptional scholar who can define the next generation of human-aware, hardware-grounded AI systems. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research develops predictive models that enable robots, intelligent products, and embodied agents to understand human intent, anticipate motion, reason about 3D environments, and act safely in real time. The successful candidate will build a rigorous and externally funded research programme that connects deep generative modelling, physical reasoning, human motion understanding, robot learning, and design-led engineering. Strategic Context EPD is a multidisciplinary pillar focused on designing and building intelligent, technology-intensive products that work in the real world. The pillar brings together strengths in robotics, electronics, design science, systems and control, materials, healthcare engineering, manufacturing, and AI-enabled product development. This search is intended to strengthen EPD’s emerging capability in physical AI: systems that can sense, model, decide, and act in human-centred environments while respecting physical, safety, and design constraints. Research Areas of Interest We welcome applicants working at the intersection of human-centric AI, embodied perception, generative world models, and robot control. Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to, 3D digital humans and expressive body models; egocentric or first-person embodied perception; synthetic data generation for embodied AI; human motion and intent prediction; action-conditioned video or latent world models; physics-compliant motion generation; whole-body control; hierarchical planning for robots in human environments; safe robot learning; and the translation of generative models into reliable physical systems. Candidate Profile Strong applicants will demonstrate a clear research vision and a publication record in leading venues in robotics, computer vision, machine learning, graphics, human motion modelling, or related fields. The search is motivated by the calibre and direction of emerging scholars whose work spans egocentric synthetic data for embodied perception, predictive world models for realistic human motion, text-conditioned and physics-compliant motion synthesis, real-world whole-body control, and safe planning for robots operating in human-centric environments. We are seeking candidates who can turn these advances into a coherent research agenda that is technically deep, externally visible, and well aligned with SUTD’s design-centric mission. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to establish an internationally recognised research group; secure competitive external research funding; publish in high-impact venues; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas such as robotics, AI, machine learning, design of intelligent products, sensing and control, or embodied systems; supervise undergraduate, Master’s, and PhD students; contribute to project-based and design-led education; and collaborate across EPD, other SUTD pillars, industry, and public-sector partners. Qualifications Applicants should have relevant expertise and experience in Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, Electrical Engineering, Applied Mathematics, Design, or a closely related field. They should show evidence of research excellence, independence, and the ability to work across disciplinary boundaries. Teaching experience, experience mentoring students, demonstrated engagement with real-world systems, and a credible plan for research translation, collaboration, or impact will be viewed favourably. Why SUTD EPD. This position offers an opportunity to shape a distinctive research and education agenda in physical AI within a design-centric engineering environment. The successful candidate will join a pillar that values technical depth, hands-on creation, interdisciplinary collaboration, and human-centred innovation, and will contribute to preparing future engineers who can design intelligent products and systems for complex real-world settings. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Senior-Research-Fellow-138682/59376244/": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow",
      "description": "Senior Research Fellow Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Senior Research Fellow Job Req ID: 2572 Employee Category: Research Department: HASS Senior Research Fellow in Buddhist Studies The Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences department at the Singapore University of Technology and Design invites applications for the position of Senior Research Fellow in Buddhist Studies. During the two-year contract, the selected candidate will contribute to a research project on pre-colonial Buddhist moral philosophy in Southeast Asia. This project will begin on 1 November 2026. Senior Research Fellow’s Responsibilities include: Digitising palmleaf manuscripts held in temple archives in northern Thailand and Laos. Interviewing the custodians of these archives and monastic experts. Reading traditional Thai and Lao materials related to Buddhist ethics (both in print and on palmleaf manuscripts). Conducting historical research and co-authoring publications. Qualifications and Competencies: Ph.D. in Buddhist Studies, Asian Studies, or another relevant discipline (essential) Proficiency in spoken and written Thai and Lao, together with the ability to read Tham, Khom and Burmese scripts, is essential as the role involve interviewing archive custodians and monastic experts, and analysing primary manuscript sources written in these languages and scripts (essential) Ability to read Pali or Sanskrit as these languages may be relevant for interpreting source materials (desirable) Experience in the digitization of palmleaf manuscripts (desirable) Interested applicants should contact Alastair Gornall ( alastair_gornall@sutd.edu.sg ) with a CV, the contact details of two referees, and a short letter of application. The deadline for applications is 1 October 2026. We will notify the candidates selected for an interview by 5 October 2026. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Researchers Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-Educator-Track-%28Engineering-Product-Development%29-138682/47673344/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member",
      "description": "Faculty Member - Educator-Track (Engineering Product Development) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member - Educator-Track (Engineering Product Development) Job Req ID: 2228 Employee Category: Faculty Department: EPD Pillar Job Description The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) is a young and innovative university with a unique educational structure and a mission to create a better world by design. Established in 2009 as Singapore’s fourth public university, in collaboration with MIT and Zhejiang University, SUTD is recognised for its innovative, active-based learning pedagogy and an interdisciplinary pillar organisation. With a stellar faculty, a small student-to-faculty ratio, and a beautiful campus, SUTD aims to nurture future technological leaders in engineering and architecture. At SUTD, technology and design education are paramount. Our pedagogy integrates engineering principles and design thinking throughout the undergraduate curriculum. More than just interdisciplinary, our courses bridge multiple dimensions of learning (D) in a unique 1-D, 2-D, and 3-D project-based framework. This position offers an exciting and unique opportunity to contribute to and shape the electrical and electronics design area within the Engineering Product Development (EPD) Pillar at SUTD. You will interact with leading stakeholders in Singapore’s engineering and innovation ecosystem, including governmental bodies, funding agencies, and industry partners who value design innovation and design thinking as key drivers of next-generation product development. Role and Responsibilities Teach electrical and electronic engineering design and product development at undergraduate, graduate, and professional levels. This could include fundamental circuit design, analog/digital electronics, embedded systems, power systems, control systems, prototyping, and testing. Develop and deliver high-quality, student-centered courses using active- and blended-learning pedagogies, with particular emphasis on electronic circuit design, product innovation, and systems-level electrical engineering. Engage in curricular development and continuous education to incorporate emerging trends in electrical engineering (e.g., renewable energy and power electronics, microcontrollers and IoT, signal processing, AI-driven circuit/system optimisation, sustainable energy systems). Collaborate with colleagues in interdisciplinary projects and research endeavours, contributing electrical engineering expertise to solve complex technological and societal challenges. Mentor and supervise students at all levels (Bachelor’s, Master’s, Doctoral) on design projects and research, fostering innovation, hands-on learning, and industry relevance. Drive outreach and partnerships with industry, funding agencies, and other academic institutions to expand SUTD’s electrical engineering initiatives, secure research funding, and develop continuous learning programmes. Becoming part of SUTD If you have a passion for teaching, a drive to advance electrical and electronic engineering research, and a desire to shape future leaders in technology and innovation, you will find a supportive environment at SUTD. You will work alongside faculty from diverse backgrounds to collaborate on curriculum and research in circuits, electronics, power systems, embedded systems, and allied areas. Whether you are just beginning your career or looking to further develop your academic profile, SUTD provides a vibrant platform to leave your mark on electrical and electronic engineering education and research – especially in areas aligned with SUTD’s strategic growth domains (Sustainability, Smart Cities, Aviation, Healthcare, and AI). The minimal qualifications for the faculty position include: A proven record of teaching and/or research in areas such as circuit design, electronics, embedded systems, power systems, signal processing, or related electrical topics. Relevant industry experience in these domains will also be considered. An appetite for improving the teaching and learning of design processes in the context of electrical and electronic product development, including hardware, systems integration, and emerging applications. A willingness to tackle complex problems in electrical/electronic engineering and design research, potentially spanning across multiple application disciplines such as energy, communications, automation, or robotics. The ability to interact effectively both face-to-face and virtually with students, peers, and all relevant stakeholders. The drive to network and engage with funding agencies, industry partners, and professional bodies, and to create impactful collaborations and continuous learning programmes. Excellent communication and presentation skills. For the Senior Lecturer position, prior teaching experience is required, with preference for candidates who have experience in technology-enabled learning, blended or active pedagogies, and/or prior involvement in engineering education research. The candidate can have: Experience in teaching in other educational environments, such as executive education and/or lifelong learning. Experience in designing and delivering short, medium and semester-long courses in various electrical and electronics topics. A track record of advising Doctoral, Master, and undergraduate students in electrical or electronics engineering. Publications in electrical and electronics engineering journals (e.g., IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems, IEEE Transactions on Power Electronics, IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics, IEEE Transactions on Smart Grid, IEEE Transactions on Control Systems Technology, IET Power Electronics, and similar) and conferences (e.g., IEEE International Symposium on Circuits and Systems (ISCAS), IEEE Power & Energy Society General Meeting, IEEE International Conference on Power Electronics and Drive Systems (PEDS), IEEE International Conference on Electronics, Circuits and Systems (ICECS), European Conference on Power Electronics and Applications (EPE), and similar). Requirements Please submit your full application package which should include: Statement of interest / Cover letter Teaching statement and prior teaching experience Past student feedback, if applicable Research statement (prior research) Full resume with profile and publication list Sample of published works Contact information of 3 referees Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Research-Assistant-138682/55655344/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research Assistant Job Req ID: 2440 Employee Category: Research Department: Future Comms R&D Programme About the Job You will conduct original research to design, analyze, and optimize communication systems, including wireless and RF technologies. You will develop novel algorithms and system architectures, perform theoretical analysis and simulation-based validation, and contribute to the advancement of next-generation cellular and satellite communication solutions. You are expected to publish findings in top-tier conferences and journals and contribute to 6G standardization activities. Who We're Looking For Bachelor's or Master's degree in Communication Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or related field. Research experience in wireless communication systems, protocols, and standards (e.g., 3GPP), with demonstrated contributions to the field. Proficiency in C, Python, and MATLAB for system modeling, simulation, and research prototyping. Experience with SDR (Software Defined Radio) concepts and lab equipment for experimental research and validation. Experience with protocol implementation and bridging (e.g., JESD204C/eCPRI), and CUDA coding for GPU acceleration. Knowledge of RF calibration, test automation, and signal integrity in a research or prototyping context. Track record of peer-reviewed publications in relevant venues (e.g., IEEE, ACM) is highly valued. Familiarity with embedded Linux and FPGA/RTL development. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and documentation skills. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Researchers Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Research-Assistant-138682/55654944/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research Assistant Job Req ID: 2438 Employee Category: Research Department: Future Comms R&D Programme About the Job You will conduct research and develop novel software solutions for real-world embedded devices and custom hardware platforms. You will design and prototype experimental systems, investigate new algorithms and architectures, and work closely with hardware and system research teams to advance the state of the art in next-generation communication systems. You are expected to publish findings in top-tier conferences and journals and contribute to 6G standardization activities. Who We're Looking For Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, or a STEM discipline. Research experience (academic or industrial) in embedded systems, communication systems, or related areas is required. Development experience in C, C++, Python, and MATLAB. Experience with embedded or low-level systems development with proven examples. Developed, debugged, and deployed software for real-world embedded devices, with a focus on research prototyping and experimental validation. Creative approach to problem solving, exceptional analytical skills, and strong engineering fundamentals. Solid knowledge of networking protocols (e.g., 3GPP), electronics, mathematics, physics, and radio frequency. Strong skills in debugging, performance optimization, and testing. Experience with large-scale C++ projects and version management tools (e.g., GitHub). Experience with STM32 microcontrollers and Xilinx RFSoC platforms, and CUDA coding for GPU acceleration. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Researchers Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Research-Assistant-138682/55655244/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research Assistant Job Req ID: 2439 Employee Category: Research Department: Future Comms R&D Programme About the Job You will conduct research into novel electronic circuit architectures and systems for advanced communication platforms. You will design and validate experimental hardware prototypes, explore emerging device technologies, and collaborate with cross-functional research teams to push the boundaries of hardware performance. You are expected to publish findings in top-tier conferences and journals and contribute to 6G standardization activities. Who We're looking For Bachelor's or Master's degree in Electrical Engineering or related field. Research experience in electronic circuit design, PCB layout, and hardware prototyping, with demonstrated ability to conduct independent research. Proficiency with lab equipment, measurement instrumentation, and debugging tools for experimental validation. Experience with embedded systems and hardware/software integration in a research or prototyping context. Experience with FPGA/RTL development and Xilinx tools, and CUDA coding for GPU acceleration. Knowledge of RF design, signal integrity, and calibration, with experience contributing to novel research outcomes. Track record of peer-reviewed publications in relevant venues (e.g., IEEE) is highly valued. Familiarity with STM32 microcontrollers and RFSoC platforms. Strong documentation and communication skills. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Researchers Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Research-Fellow-I-138682/55655744/": {
      "title": "Research Fellow I",
      "description": "Research Fellow I Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research Fellow I Job Req ID: 2441 Employee Category: Research Department: Future Comms R&D Programme About the Job You will lead and shape the research agenda of the lab, oversee R&D activities, and build and manage high-performing research teams. The role will define research directions, drive publication strategies, mentor researchers, foster collaboration with academic and industry partners, and ensure the successful execution of research programs in advanced communication systems. Who We're Looking For Master’s or PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Communication Engineering, Computer Science, or related field. Proven track record of research contributions in wireless communication technologies, including peer-reviewed publications and/or patents. Experience in research team management, project coordination, and cross-site academic-industry collaboration. Deep understanding of mobile communication systems and standards (3G/4G/5G/6G), with a strong publication record in one or more of these areas. Expertise and demonstrated research contributions in areas such as AI for wireless communication, satellite communication systems, or energy engineering for wireless networks. Experience securing research funding, managing research programs, and building academic partnerships. Experience with embedded systems, FPGA/RTL, and RF technologies, and CUDA coding for GPU acceleration is a plus. Strong leadership, communication, and documentation skills. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Researchers Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Writing-Specialist-%28Part-Time%29-138682/47279344/": {
      "title": "Writing Specialist (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Writing Specialist (Part-Time) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Writing Specialist (Part-Time) Job Req ID: 2106 Employee Category: Admin Department: Office of Education & Innovation Communication Specialist, Centre for Writing and Rhetoric The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) is Singapore’s fourth university with a focus on design and multidisciplinary curriculum and research. Students collaborate in multidisciplinary teams for their assignments and Capstone projects. SUTD’s Centre for Writing and Rhetoric (CWR) offers English and communication programmes as part of the engineering and architecture degrees and within the Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences cluster. Responsibilities Teach specific writing and speaking skills in different disciplines Provide relevant material to enhance (online) writing and presentation skills Provide meaningful and timely feedback to students during consultation sessions Administer tests and other assessment tools Attend standardization and faculty meetings Qualifications M.A. in applied linguistics, English language, communication studies, linguistics OR PhD in an academic field (e.g. humanities and social sciences) 1to 3 years of experience in teaching general communication course and/or discipline-specific communication courses in engineering, humanities, and social sciences, at university level OTHER INFORMATION Can didates must have a degree from an accredited institution and have not been conferred honorary degrees. If you meet the criteria, we invite you to submit a résumé , copies of your transcripts, and recent student evaluations (if applicable). Candidates who do not possess the stipulated qualifications but have relevant industrial experience (e.g. in professional communication) may still apply. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Admin Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Deputy-Manager-138682/55203044/": {
      "title": "Deputy Manager",
      "description": "Deputy Manager Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Deputy Manager Job Req ID: 2363 Employee Category: Admin Department: Office of Research Job Title: Deputy Manager (Contract) Department: Office of Research About Office of Research The Office of Research advances the university’s status as the world's first Design∙AI university by fostering a strong culture of research excellence and interdisciplinary collaboration, focusing on high‑quality transformative research that integrates human‑centred design, advanced technologies, and responsible innovation. What You’ll Do You will manage the day-to-day operations of the Office of Research, which includes but is not limited to the following: Provide end-to-end support to faculty for pre- and post-award management in a timely and accurate manner and advise on institutional processes/policies and funding agencies’ requirements. Build and maintain strong working relationships with internal and external stakeholders to advance the University’s research agenda. Manage research grant processes to ensure compliance with institutional policies and funding agencies’ guidelines. Maintain appropriate governance, documentation, and process controls to support auditability and good grant management stewardship. Manage day‑to‑day grants system activities, coordinate system updates across stakeholders, deliver research reporting and analytics, and support workflow standardisation and automation within grant administration. Provide secretariat support for meetings organised by the Office of Research where required. Who We Are Looking For A Bachelor in a scientific/technical discipline At least 3 years of relevant experience in grant and/or project management Strong knowledge and understanding of Singapore’s R&D and funding landscape (e.g. MOE, NRF, A*STAR grants) Highly detail-oriented with the ability to multi-task in a dynamic working environment and meet tight deadlines A strong sense of ownership and able to autonomously carry forward key aspects of work Work well both independently and within a team Possesses strong interpersonal, communication, and analytical skill Skilled in Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint Apply now » Find similar jobs: Admin Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-Tenure-Track-%28Design-and-Artificial-Intelligence%29-138682/22388544/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track (Design and Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track (Design and Artificial Intelligence) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member - Tenure-Track (Design and Artificial Intelligence) Job Req ID: 1523 Employee Category: Faculty Department: Design&Artificial Intelligence - Undergraduates The Role This position constitutes a very exciting and unique opportunity to mature with, and help shape the design area at SUTD. Along the way, the candidate will interact with the governing bodies in Singapore, the funding agencies and the industrial eco-system. The successful candidate will work across all areas of academic activity: education, research, service to the university, and outreach. The candidate will be part of an innovative team, where he/she will utilise his/her demonstrated skills in blended learning to develop and deliver high-quality student-centred undergraduate and postgraduate programs. He/she will make a positive contribution to an already established innovation culture and mindset for students at all levels, and engage and work with industry on challenging research problems. The candidate will engage in engineering  design research and teaching  at all levels, from first-year undergraduate to PhD level, in multiple design courses, either co-teaching, leading a team of colleagues, or being the sole instructor. Courses that have to do with topics like Engineering Design Innovation, Design Thinking, and Design Science (to name just a few) from an Engineering perspective, heavy on research tools and research methods. Becoming part of SUTD With a passion for teaching and a flair for research in Engineering Design, you will meet with colleagues from all backgrounds to collaborate and develop your own niche in engineering design research. You will have the opportunity to leave your own mark by understanding what others have done before you, and the work they have developed up to now, and consequently contribute with your own vision of multidisciplinary design teaching and convergent engineering design research. Design is taught at all levels of higher education, including adult and executive learning . Building or strengthening a research interest around the teaching of technically grounded design or the application of design in engineering to the growth areas defined at SUTD (Sustainability, Cities, Aviation, Healthcare, and AI) will enable you to connect with all relevant stakeholders in and around SUTD. Requirements The candidate must have A PhD in Engineering, with a proven record of teaching and research in engineering design and related topics Proven experience in working autonomously and in teams, multi-tasking between teaching and research An appetite for improving teaching and learning of engineering design A willingness to tackle complex problems in engineering design research, potentially spanning across multiple application domains The ability to interact both face-to-face as well as virtually with students, peers, and all relevant stakeholders The drive to network and engage with funding agencies and companies, and secure the necessary funding to conduct research and build a well-connected research team The candidate can have: Experience in teaching in other educational environments, like executive education and/or lifelong learning Experience in designing and delivering short courses in various design-related topics A track record of advising Doctoral, Master, and undergraduate students in engineering design research Publications in leading engineering design research journals (e.g., Research in Engineering Design, Journal of Engineering Design, Design Science, Journal of Mechanical Design, Artificial Intelligence for Engineering Design, Analysis and Manufacturing, and similar) and conferences (International Conference on Engineering Design, International Design Engineering Technical Conference, International DESIGN Conference, and similar) Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Research-Associate-138682/59177744/": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Research Associate Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research Associate Job Req ID: 2567 Employee Category: Research Department: HASS Research Associate: Social Science of Human-Wildlife Interactions Join an interdisciplinary research team investigating the human activities that create exposure risks for zoonotic disease spillover from wild mammals in Singapore. Funded by a Biosurveillance Research Grant from the National Parks Board, this role will support Associate Professor Lyle Fearnley, a medical anthropologist, in advancing research at the intersection of social science, public health, wildlife, and environmental change. The Research Associate, or Senior Research Assistant, should have academic training in anthropology, sociology, or a related discipline. The candidate must demonstrate experience and proven ability in designing and conducting qualitative interviews, as well as applying other qualitative social science research methods. Preferred Experience Familiarity with designing and analysing quantitative surveys Experience contributing to journal articles in the social sciences or interdisciplinary fields Interest in wildlife, anthropogenic environmental change, or One Health issues The Research Associate will be based at SUTD and will work closely with a highly interdisciplinary research team. The team includes microbiologists, wildlife specialists, data modellers, and social scientists from SUTD, NTU’s Asian School of the Environment, and the Singapore Centre for Environmental Life Sciences Engineering. This is an opportunity to contribute to pioneering research in the One Health social sciences and to help advance understanding of the links between human activity, wildlife, and zoonotic disease risk in Singapore. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Researchers Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-%28Architecture-and-Sustainable-Design%29-Architectural-and-Urban-Design-138682/16429244/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design)",
      "description": "Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design) - Architectural and Urban Design Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design) - Architectural and Urban Design Job Req ID: 1260 Employee Category: Faculty Department: ASD Pillar The Role This position constitutes a very exciting and unique opportunity to mature with and help shape the design area at SUTD. Along the way, the candidate will interact with the governing bodies in Singapore, the funding agencies and the industrial eco-system. The successful candidate will work across all areas of academic activity: education, research, service to the university, and outreach. The candidate will be part of an innovative team, where he/she will utilise his/her demonstrated skills in blended learning to develop and deliver high-quality student-centred undergraduate and postgraduate programs. He/she will make a positive contribution to an already established innovation culture and mindset for students at all levels, and engage and work with industry on challenging research problems. The candidate will engage in research on ergonomic design and teaching at all levels, from first-year undergraduate to PhD level, in multiple design courses, either co-teaching, leading a team of colleagues, or being the sole instructor. Becoming part of SUTD With a passion for teaching and a flair for research in Design, you will meet with colleagues from all backgrounds to collaborate and develop your own niche in design research. You will have the opportunity to leave your own mark by understanding what others have done before you, and the work they have developed up to now, and consequently contribute with your own vision of multidisciplinary design teaching and convergent design research. Design is taught at all levels of higher education, including adult and executive learning . Building or strengthening a research interest around the teaching of technically grounded design or the application of design innovation to the growth areas defined at SUTD (Sustainability, Cities, Aviation, Healthcare, and AI) will enable you to connect with all relevant stakeholders in and around SUTD. Requirements The candidate must have Specialty in Ergonomics or related areas, with a proven record of teaching and research in design and related topics Proven experience in working autonomously and in teams, multi-tasking between teaching and research An appetite for improving teaching and learning of design A willingness to tackle complex problems in design research, potentially spanning across multiple application domains The ability to interact both face-to-face as well as virtually with students, peers, and all relevant stakeholders The drive to network and engage with funding agencies and companies, and secure the necessary funding to conduct research and build a well-connected research team The candidate can have: Experience in teaching in other educational environments, like executive education and/or lifelong learning Experience in designing and delivering short courses in various design-related topics A track record of advising Doctoral, Master, and undergraduate students in design research Publications in leading design research journals (e.g., Research in Engineering Design, Journal of Engineering Design, Design Science, Journal of Mechanical Design, Artificial Intelligence for Engineering Design, Analysis and Manufacturing, and similar) and conferences (International Conference on Engineering Design, International Design Engineering Technical Conference, International DESIGN Conference, and similar) Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-%28Design-and-Artificial-Intelligence%29-138682/16414744/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member (Design and Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Faculty Member (Design and Artificial Intelligence) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member (Design and Artificial Intelligence) Job Req ID: 1259 Employee Category: Faculty Department: Design&Artificial Intelligence - Undergraduates The Role The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) is seeking applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in the interdisciplinary field of Human-Centred Design and Artificial Intelligence (AI). We are looking for candidates with a robust research background and teaching experience in areas that intersect design, AI, and technology. This position offers a unique and exciting opportunity to shape and advance the field of human-centred design and AI at SUTD The successful candidate will be responsible for conducting cutting-edge research in human-centred design and AI, with a focus on how AI technologies—such as natural language processing, computer vision and sensors—can be leveraged to enhance the human condition. The candidate will contribute to advancing the Design and Artificial Intelligence Programme’s mission by integrating human-centred design, AI, and emerging technologies to tackle complex, real-world challenges. The role encompasses all areas of academic activity, including education, research, service to the university, and outreach. The candidate will join a dynamic and innovative team, utilising their expertise in blended learning to develop and deliver high-quality, student-centred undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Additionally, the candidate will contribute to fostering an innovative culture and mindset among students and engage with industry partners on challenging research problems Becoming part of SUTD With a passion for teaching and a strong research focus in human-centred design and AI, you will collaborate with colleagues from diverse backgrounds to develop your niche in this interdisciplinary field. You will have the opportunity to build upon existing research while contributing your own vision to the evolving landscape of human-centred design and AI. Design is taught across all levels of higher education at SUTD, including adult and executive learning. By building or enhancing a research interest around the teaching of technically grounded design or the application of design in engineering to SUTD’s growth areas—Sustainability, Cities, Aviation, Healthcare, and AI—you will have the opportunity to connect with a wide range of stakeholders within and beyond the university. About SUTD The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) is a leading institution Singapore that emphasises human-centred design, technology, innovation and entrepreneurship. SUTD’s Design and Artificial Intelligence Programme is at the forefront of designing cutting-edge AI technologies focused on people, and preparing students to lead in a rapidly evolving technological landscape. The Programme is committed to pioneering research and education in areas like human-computer interaction, pervasive sensing systems, and AI-driven design solutions that address the complex challenges of the future. Responsibilities Lead, conduct, and publish high-impact research at the intersection of design, AI, pervasive sensing systems, and human-computer interaction (HCI). Secure research funding through competitive grants and collaborations with industry partners. Supervise and mentor undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students in research projects. Develop and deliver undergraduate and graduate courses in computer science, human-centred design, and AI. Contribute to the strategic direction and administration of the DAI Programme and the university. Lead and participate in initiatives that align with SUTD’s strategic goals in design, AI, and technology. Requirements We encourage candidates with the following qualifications to apply: A Ph.D. in a relevant field, such as Human-Computer Interaction, Human-Centred Design, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Pervasive Computing, or a closely related discipline. A strong research portfolio demonstrated through publications in reputable journals and conferences. Evidence of teaching excellence and a commitment to innovative pedagogy. Preferably experience in securing research funding Experience leading research projects. Ability to work collaboratively in an interdisciplinary environment. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. A passion for integrating human-centred design, AI, pervasive sensing systems to solve complex, real-world problems. A mindset of continual growth and academic excellence Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Members-Educator-Track-%28Information-Systems-Technology-and-Design%29-138682/13766744/": {
      "title": "Faculty Members",
      "description": "Faculty Members - Educator-Track (Information Systems Technology and Design) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Members - Educator-Track (Information Systems Technology and Design) Job Req ID: 589 Employee Category: Faculty Department: ISTD Pillar Job Description The Information Systems Technology and Design (ISTD) Pillar seeks applications to fill several educator track faculty positions in the following areas: Software Engineering. Security Robotics Successful candidate(s) will be expected to teach courses in one of these areas at the undergraduate level. Candidate should also have the technical background to teach introductory programming classes and at least two of the core Computer Science and Design (CSD) pillar courses. Opportunities to teach at the Master's level or continuing education and training programmes may also be available. Further details on the CSD core curriculum can be found at the SUTD CSD curriculum website. Prior experience in one or more of the following areas will be considered a strong advantage: Common Area: Teaching and pedagogy Design thinking Software Engineering: Agile software engineering Software design and architecture Agentic software development Security: Network and system security Network protocol level encryption Systems and networking basics Blockchain security Robotics: Machine Learning Computer Vision Robot Control System Depending on the candidate’s prior teaching experience, the appointment may be at the level of Lecturer or Senior Lecturer. Candidates with at least 10 years of teaching experience in Computer Science will also be considered. The initial appointment is for up to three years and is renewable, subject to satisfactory performance. Teaching at SUTD is both challenging and deeply rewarding. Faculty on the educator track play a central role in shaping the next generation of computing professionals, with a primary focus on delivering and managing undergraduate courses. The teaching load is higher than that of tenure-track faculty, but so is the opportunity to make a direct and lasting impact on students’ learning and growth. In addition to teaching, faculties contribute through service to SUTD and the broader community. Performance is evaluated with an emphasis on teaching excellence, giving dedicated educators the chance to be recognised and advanced for the quality of their teaching. Successful candidates should therefore have a passion for teaching and a strong desire to nurture the next generation of Computer Science graduates. Qualified applicants will be invited for an on-site interview which will include a short micro-teaching segment to demonstrate their teaching abilities and passion for education. For applicants based overseas who are unable to attend in person, interviews may be conducted online. In such cases, candidates may also be asked to submit a recorded microteaching segment with specific requirements communicated separately. SUTD is a design-focused university offering five majors or “pillars” with a relatively small annual undergraduate intake. Our undergraduate education emphasises a cohort-based active learning pedagogy, where faculty engage students through interactive lessons in classes of around fifty. Project-based and interdisciplinary learning are core features of the curriculum, providing students with hands-on experience and broad exposure across domains. Our undergraduate curriculum has a unique structure, where students do three terms of common courses before embarking on their chosen major, culminating in an industry-focused group-based interdisciplinary capstone project. Beyond teaching, SUTD is also home to world-class centres of excellence in multi-disciplinary research, including the iTrust Center for Research in Cyber Security, the Lee Kuan Yew Centre for Innovative Cities (LKYCIC), and the AI Mega Centre. Successful candidates can look forward to internationally competitive remuneration, and relocation support for those moving to Singapore. If you share SUTD’s vision on multi-disciplinary education and research with a strong emphasis on “Design” in the broadest sense, we invite you to apply. Job Requirements Please submit a complete application package that includes: Full resume (with profile, publications, and conference papers) Statement of interest / Cover letter Teaching philosophy / statement Two letters of reference Evidence of past teaching experience, if available (e.g. teaching evaluations or feedback) Additional supporting documents (such as sample syllabi or teaching portfolios) may also be included For inquiries about the position, please contact istd@sutd.edu.sg . Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-%28Architecture-and-Sustainable-Design%29-Building-Science-and-Technology-138682/13766544/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design)",
      "description": "Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design) - Building Science and Technology Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member (Architecture and Sustainable Design) - Building Science and Technology Job Req ID: 971 Employee Category: Faculty Department: ASD Pillar Position Description The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate expertise in the areas of building science and technology, with emphasis in architectural tectonics, sustainable materials and methods of construction, application of innovative digital design technologies for assessment of building performance and a vision the future of architectural building design and production. Candidates are expected to teach undergraduate courses in architectural tectonics, design for manufacturing and assembly, including selection of building materials, pre-fabricated and on-site methods of construction, as well as technical documentation of architectural design for construction. In addition, candidates will propose and develop an elective offered to both undergraduate and graduate students stemming from their research work as means of creating a conduit between advanced research and architectural education. Candidates will be expected to conduct research and/or produce creative work within a research-intensive university setting, seek for research funding from relevant government and industry sources and contribute to building science and technology via academic publishing in international journals and conference proceedings and/or relevant demonstrative work. Requirements Specialty in building science and technology or significant architectural practice experience on relevant areas Academic or professional publications of research or applied work in building science and technology Awards for teaching and/or design Previous academic teaching and/or professional experience (with examples) Demonstration of research and/or creative work Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Members-Tenure-Track-%28Information-Systems-Technology-and-Design%29-138682/13766844/": {
      "title": "Faculty Members - Tenure-Track  (Information Systems Technology and Design)",
      "description": "Faculty Members - Tenure-Track  (Information Systems Technology and Design) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Members - Tenure-Track  (Information Systems Technology and Design) Job Req ID: 594 Employee Category: Faculty Department: ISTD Pillar Job Description The Information Systems Technology and Design (ISTD) Pillar invites applications to fill several Tenure Track faculty positions. Appointments will be at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Highly qualified applicants with a substantial track record of research accomplishments, an active research program, and strong teaching experience may be considered for appointment as Tenured Full Professor. Faculty duties include teaching subjects at the undergraduate and graduate levels, research, supervision of students, advising undergraduate student projects, and service to SUTD and the community. Candidates for senior positions must demonstrate the ability to successfully create and manage an independent research program. Exceptional candidates in all areas will be considered, but priority will be given to those in the following areas. Artificial intelligence (with a focus on Machine Learning, Multi-agent Systems) Systems and networking Cyber security Established in collaboration with MIT, SUTD is the proud host of several world-class centres of excellence in multi-disciplinary research, including the SUTD-MIT International Design Centre (IDC), iTrust Centre for cybersecurity research, Future Communications R&D Programme, Lee Kuan Yew Centre for Innovative Cities (LKYCIC), Digital Manufacturing and Design (DManD) Centre, and Temasek Labs. Successful candidates can expect internationally competitive remuneration (commensurate with qualifications), assistance for relocation to Singapore, and an attractive startup package for research. Singapore offers many opportunities for external research grants for individual or team-based projects. If you share SUTD’s vision for multi-disciplinary curricula and research with a focus on “Design” in the broadest sense, please contact us. For further information, visit https://www.sutd.edu.sg/istd/ or https://www.sutd.edu.sg . Job Requirements Please submit your full application package, it should include: A cover letter Full resume (with research interest, list of publications) Research statement Teaching statement 3 representative research papers Names of 3 references (this should be mentioned in the resume) Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-AssociateSenior-Associate-%28Hard-Facilities-Management-Mechanical-Engineering%29-138682/25040844/": {
      "title": "Associate/Senior Associate (Hard Facilities Management",
      "description": "Associate/Senior Associate (Hard Facilities Management - Mechanical Engineering) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Associate/Senior Associate (Hard Facilities Management - Mechanical Engineering) Job Req ID: 1567 Employee Category: Admin Department: Campus Infra & Facilities Associate/Senior Associate (Hard Facilities Management – Mechanical Engineering) - Contract Position Why You’ll Love This Role You will be part of the Facilities Management team in the Office of Campus Infrastructure and Facilities (OCIF) and be responsible for the management and maintenance of the campus facilities. You will report to a Manager and work together with our out-sourced service providers to ensure that the day-to-day management of facilities, maintenance support services, processes and frameworks and delivery of key performance indicators (KPI) are consistently kept at a high standard to support our campus operational requirements. What You’ll Do Assist the Manager to maintain the operational readiness, safe and efficient operation of the campus M&E services; Manage good rapport with internal stakeholders and attend to their maintenance feedback and requests for improvement works; Carry out procurement of goods and services for maintenance and improvement works based on the University’s procurement policy including preparation of requirement specifications, evaluation and drafting the recommendation report; Manage the contract administration process including meeting contractual obligations, specification reviews and timely verification & payment of term contract and ad hoc Invoices including verifying works done; Consolidate and update the PPM Schedule for the team; Ensure timely renewal of licenses for all operating systems; Carry out routine check on all common M&E services to ensure operations timing are based on approved schedule, and their operations/ conditions are within acceptable level; Coordinate, supervise and certify maintenance activities to ensure contractors/vendors complete all repair and maintenance work within the required timelines and standards; Ensure compliance of OCIF procedures and checklists; Regularly check on maintenance stock inventory and ensure timely replenishment; Manage PTW; Conduct system audit and site inspections; Provide project management support for fit-outs, renovations and upgrading works to ensure timely completion of projects and meet the University's house rules, requirement specifications and quality standards; Follow up on defect rectification works. Provide advice and support for University research or academic projects, when required; Work as part of the cross-functional team in supporting soft services, security, civil works and engineering services functions; Preparation of management reports and tracking of KPIs; Other duties as assigned by the Manager. Who We Are Looking For Degree/ Diploma in Facilities Management, Engineering (Electrical/ Mechanical) or equivalent; At least 2 years (4 years for Diploma) of experience in performing maintenance works on Mechanical System especially relating to air-conditioning & mechanical ventilation, water-cooled and air-cooled chilled system, fire protection/detection system, pumping system and building management system, preferably in institutional, educational, research or large scale commercial developments; Familiar with local Code of Practices, Building and Fire Safety regulations; Conversant in reading and interpreting architectural and M&E schematic drawings; Conversant in Microsoft Office and AutoCAD.  Ability to use 3D perspective drawing software such as Sketch-up will be an added advantage; Working experience in the BCA GreenMark certification and/or sustainability-related projects (such as Solar PV systems, EV charging solutions, District Cooling, etc.) will be an added advantage. Excellent verbal and written communication skills and inter-personnel skills with the ability to communicate effectively across all levels and function well in a team. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Admin Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-Tenure-TrackTenured-%28Engineering-Product-Development%29-138682/48334144/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track/Tenured (Engineering Product Development)",
      "description": "Faculty Member - Tenure-Track/Tenured (Engineering Product Development) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member - Tenure-Track/Tenured (Engineering Product Development) Job Req ID: 2260 Employee Category: Faculty Department: EPD Pillar The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) is a young and innovative university with a unique educational structure and a mission to create a better world by design. Established in 2009 as Singapore’s fourth public university, in collaboration with MIT and Zhejiang University, SUTD is recognised for its innovative, active-based learning pedagogy and an interdisciplinary pillar organisation. With a stellar faculty, a small student-to-faculty ratio, and a beautiful campus, SUTD aims to nurture future technological leaders in engineering and architecture. At SUTD, technology and design education are paramount. Our pedagogy integrates engineering principles and design thinking throughout the undergraduate curriculum. More than just interdisciplinary, our courses bridge multiple dimensions of learning (D) in a unique 1-D, 2-D, and 3-D project-based framework. MIT News Article on SUTD’s Engineering Education About the Position SUTD’s Engineering Product Development (EPD) Pillar invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position specialising in Aerial Robotics . We seek candidates with expertise in emerging aerial robotic systems, including multirotor drones, flapping-wing (bio-inspired) UAVs, morphing aerial structures, aerial manipulation platforms, and other novel flight systems. This position offers an exciting opportunity to lead cutting-edge research and education in the field of aerial robotics within SUTD’s cross-disciplinary, design-centric ecosystem. The successful candidate will collaborate with a dynamic team of faculty across multiple engineering disciplines and engage with Singapore’s thriving aviation and technology sectors, including government agencies, aerospace companies, and research partners, to drive innovation in next-generation aerial robotic systems. Role and Responsibilities Teaching: Teach courses in robotics and related engineering areas at the undergraduate and graduate levels. This may include topics such as aerial vehicle design, dynamics and control, mechatronics, autonomous systems, and related subjects, with an emphasis on hands-on learning and project-based work. Curriculum Development: Develop and deliver high-quality, student-centered courses and content focusing on aerial robotics. Employ active learning and design-thinking pedagogies to create immersive learning experiences in drone design, prototyping, and testing. Innovation in Aerial Robotics: Drive curricular updates and continuous education initiatives to incorporate emerging trends in aerial robotics (e.g. AI-enabled autonomous navigation, swarm robotics, flapping-wing flight, advanced materials and additive manufacturing for UAVs). Ensure that SUTD’s curriculum remains at the forefront of technological advances in this field. Interdisciplinary Collaboration: Collaborate with colleagues in interdisciplinary projects and research, contributing aerial robotics expertise to solve complex engineering challenges. Integrate mechanical, electrical, and aerospace engineering perspectives in research initiatives to develop innovative aerial robotic solutions. Student Mentorship: Mentor and supervise students at all levels (Bachelor’s, Master’s, PhD) on capstone projects and research in aerial robotics, fostering an innovative mindset and ensuring industry relevance. Guide students in designing, building, and testing novel robotic systems for real-world applications. Industry and Research Engagement: Lead outreach and partnerships with industry, government agencies, and other academic or research institutions to expand SUTD’s aerial robotics initiatives. Seek research funding and collaborative projects that enhance SUTD’s profile in drones and autonomous systems and develop opportunities for continuous learning programmes in this domain. Becoming part of SUTD If you have a passion for teaching and cutting-edge research in aerial robotics, and a desire to shape future technology leaders, you will find a supportive environment at SUTD. You will work alongside faculty from diverse backgrounds to collaborate on interdisciplinary research and curriculum initiatives in robotics, autonomous systems, and related areas. Whether you are just beginning your career or looking to further develop your academic profile, SUTD provides a vibrant platform to leave your mark on aerial robotics innovation – especially in areas aligned with the university’s strategic growth domains (Sustainability, Cities, Aviation, Healthcare, and AI). SUTD’s culture of design-centered engineering and cross-disciplinary collaboration means you will have opportunities to translate ideas into impactful solutions across various sectors. Qualifications and Attributes Candidates for this position should possess the following qualifications and attributes: Research Excellence: A strong research background in robotics – preferably with a focus on aerial robotics – demonstrated by a track record of high-quality publications, patents, and/or innovative projects. Ability to establish an independent research programme and attain research funding in the aerial robotics field. Teaching and Mentorship: Commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring. Ability to develop and teach courses in robotics and engineering design. Prior teaching experience or pedagogical training (especially in project-based learning or design innovation) is advantageous, as is any evidence of effective teaching (e.g. positive student feedback). Interdisciplinary and Design Aptitude: Genuine enthusiasm for cross-disciplinary collaboration and design-centric innovation. Willingness to integrate knowledge from mechanical, electrical, and aerospace engineering (and beyond) in both research and education. Communication and Collaboration: Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with students, colleagues, and external partners. A demonstrated ability to work in teams and contribute to a collegial academic environment. Industry Engagement: A proactive mindset for industry engagement and societal impact. Drive to collaborate with industry stakeholders and government agencies, and to translate research outcomes into real-world applications or entrepreneurship. (Prior experience in working with industry or securing industry-funded projects is a plus.) SUTD welcomes applications from both early-career researchers with exceptional potential and mid-career faculty with established track records. The appointment will be made at a rank commensurate with the candidate’s experience and accomplishments. Application Procedure Please submit a complete application package that includes the following: Cover Letter: A statement of interest highlighting your fit for the position and relevant experience in aerial robotics. Teaching Statement: Summary of teaching philosophy and experience (including prior teaching roles and any available student feedback or evaluations). Research Statement: Outline of past research accomplishments and future research plans in aerial robotics and related areas. Curriculum Vitae (CV): Full resume including academic background, appointments, list of publications, awards, and other relevant accomplishments. Sample Publications: Examples of your scholarly work (e.g. one or two representative publications in robotics or engineering). References: Contact information for three references who can comment on your research and teaching qualifications. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for interviews. The successful candidate is expected to commence employment at SUTD on a mutually agreed date. Join us at SUTD and help define the future of Aerial Robotics in an innovative, design-focused academic environment. We look forward to your application! Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Research-AssistantAssociate-138682/56751544/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate",
      "description": "Research Assistant/Associate Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research Assistant/Associate Job Req ID: 2500 Employee Category: Research Department: LKYCIC Research Assistant/Associate (Community Innovation and Applied Social Research) The Lee Kuan Yew Centre for Innovative Cities (LKYCIC) at the Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) invites applications for full-time Research Assistant/Associate appointments to support applied research and innovation projects on people, communities, and cities. The position is suited for candidates with strong interests in mixed-methods social science research, social policy innovation, community development, and translating research into real-world impact. The successful applicant will join an interdisciplinary team working at the intersection of behavioural science, urban planning, public health, sustainability, and community activation. About the role The successful candidate will contribute to projects in LKYCIC focusing on understanding how social and built environments shape individual and community outcomes, and how research can be translated into practical interventions, programmes, policies, and design solutions. Current and upcoming projects include: Social capital and community resilience in neighbourhoods and community hubs Climate adaptation, urban heat resilience, and sustainable living Community activation and citizen engagement initiatives Population health and healthy neighbourhoods Design and evaluation of community-based interventions Development of practical tools, frameworks, and guidelines for policymakers and practitioners Projects typically involve a combination of surveys, interviews, focus groups, behavioural observations, workshops, participatory design activities, and field-based research conducted in partnership with government agencies, community organisations, industry partners, and residents. Depending on the project, researchers may also have opportunities to work with digital platforms, spatial data, and emerging AI-enabled tools that support research, community engagement, programme design, and policy innovation. Key responsibilities The candidate will be expected to: Support the design and implementation of mixed-methods research studies Conduct literature reviews and evidence synthesis Design and administer surveys, interviews, focus groups, and workshops Conduct field observations and community-based data collection Analyse qualitative and quantitative data using appropriate methods and software Assist in stakeholder engagement, participatory design, and community activation activities Support project management, coordination, and reporting Prepare research reports, policy briefs, presentations, and academic manuscripts Contribute to the translation of research findings into practical recommendations, interventions, and tools Work collaboratively with interdisciplinary researchers and external partners The Centre may, at its discretion, assign additional responsibilities from time to time, such as teaching or other duties aligned with the Centre’s needs. Skills and qualifications required Bachelor’s or postgraduate degree (MA, MSc, March, MPP or equivalent) in sociology, public policy, geography, urban studies, architecture, public health, psychology, community development, social work, behavioural science, environmental studies, or related disciplines ⁠ Demonstrated interest in applied social science research, real-world impact, and the translation of research into practical interventions, programmes, policies, or design solutions Experience with qualitative and/or quantitative research methods, including survey design, interviews, focus groups, observations, workshops, or field-based research Strong analytical, organisational, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to exercise good judgement and initiative in complex real-world settings ⁠ Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to present research insights clearly to academic, policy, practitioner, and community audiences Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within interdisciplinary and partner-facing teams ⁠ Interest in community engagement, social innovation, urban issues, sustainability, public health, and/or policy development Adaptability and willingness to learn new methods, tools, and approaches, including digital platforms, spatial data, or AI-enabled research tools where relevant The following would be advantageous: Experience conducting fieldwork and community-based research Experience in programme evaluation, policy analysis, or participatory research How to apply Interested applicants are encouraged to send their application with the subject heading “Research Assistant/Associate (Community Innovation and Applied Social Research)” to lkycic@sutd.edu.sg with the following: Cover letter explaining your interest in the position and addressing the qualifications and skills requirements (maximum 1 page) Curriculum vitae Two writing sample (e.g., thesis, report, publication, policy brief, or research paper) Names and contact details of three referees who may be contacted for a reference We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and will continue until the position is filled. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Researchers Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Position-Tenure-TrackTenured-%28Engineering-Systems-and-Design%29-138682/13958844/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position",
      "description": "Faculty Position - Tenure-Track/Tenured (Engineering Systems and Design) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Position - Tenure-Track/Tenured (Engineering Systems and Design) Job Req ID: 997 Employee Category: Faculty Department: ESD Pillar Open Faculty Positions at the Engineering Systems and Design Pillar The Engineering Systems and Design (ESD) pillar within the Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) is pursuing multiple, exceptional tenure-track/tenured faculty hires at all levels. About SUTD and ESD The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) has topped the list of emerging engineering schools (MIT report, 2018) and possesses a unique structure and mission within the vibrant nation of Singapore. SUTD features the integration of design with engineering, an intimate student to faculty ratio, an innovative active learning pedagogy, an interdisciplinary pillar organization, a stellar faculty, and a beautiful new campus. The Engineering Systems and Design (ESD) pillar within SUTD offers exceptional undergraduate and doctoral degrees focusing on Business Analytics and Operations Research, Financial Services, Supply Chain and Logistics, and Aviation Systems. ESD research spans optimization, systems and control, artificial intelligence and data science, and decision-making for complex engineering systems, including robotics and autonomous systems. ESD undergraduates are prepared for a wide range of engineering and management careers in the private and public sectors, including healthcare, banking, manufacturing, supply chains, energy, transportation, entertainment, and hospitality. They are also well prepared for entrepreneurship and launching start-up ventures. Job Requirements for Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty We invite applications from exceptional candidates whose research addresses one or more of the following application domains: Aviation, with particular interest in airport operations; Supply chain and logistics; Quantitative finance and financial engineering; Healthcare analytics and operations; and Operations enabled by robotics, automation, and autonomous systems, with emphasis on operational decision-making, planning, coordination, control, optimization and deployment. Candidates should demonstrate strong methodological or computational expertise in one or more of the following areas: operations research and optimization; statistics, machine learning (ML), artificial intelligence (AI), and data science; systems theory, optimal control, and discrete-event systems; quantum computing; and high-performance computing. We welcome candidates from a broad range of disciplinary backgrounds whose research connects these methodological foundations with one or more of the application domains above. Successful candidates should be specialised in the relevant discipline. Empirical, experimental, computational, and analytical research approaches are all welcome. Candidates must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and to developing and sustaining an active research program. Successful candidates can look forward to competitive remuneration, assistance for relocation to Singapore, and attractive research start-up packages through SUTD Kickstarter Initiative (SKI) and grant opportunities. A candidate’s full application package should include: A cover letter Curriculum Vitae (CV), including publications Research statement / plans Teaching statement / plans 3 representative research papers Contact information of 3 referees How to apply Applications are being accepted online and the review of applications is ongoing. Additional information about the university and the Engineering Systems and Design pillar can be found at https://esd.sutd.edu.sg . For direct enquiries contact Associate Professor Carlos Gerardo Murguia Rendon, murguia_rendon@sutd.edu.sg. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-Practice-Track-Position-in-Business-and-AI-%28DAI%29-138682/57976944/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member - Practice-Track Position in Business and AI (DAI)",
      "description": "Faculty Member - Practice-Track Position in Business and AI (DAI) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member - Practice-Track Position in Business and AI (DAI) Job Req ID: 2540 Employee Category: Faculty Department: Design&Artificial Intelligence - Undergraduates Design and Artificial Intelligence (Supercharged DAI) & Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (HASS) The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) invites applications for a Practice-Track Faculty Position in Business and AI, jointly aligned with SUTD's Supercharged DAI initiative and the Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (HASS) cluster. We seek an experienced practitioner, industry leader, investor, entrepreneur, or practitioner-scholar who can bring strong business expertise, professional networks, and demonstrated real-world impact into SUTD's interdisciplinary and design-centric learning environment. About the Role The successful candidate will contribute to business education within SUTD's Supercharged DAI curriculum and broader HASS offerings. The role emphasizes practice-informed teaching, industry engagement, and the development of applied learning opportunities that connect business, AI, technology, design, and society. The position is intended for candidates with substantial experience in areas such as business transformation, organizational innovation, and technology adoption entrepreneurship, venture investment/building, consulting, or executive leadership. The successful candidate will help students understand how organizations, entrepreneurs, and/or investors can respond strategically, responsibly, and innovatively to the opportunities and challenges created by AI. Areas of expertise may include: AI-enabled business transformation and strategy Digital transformation and organizational innovation Leadership, change management, and technology adoption Business analytics and data-informed decision-making Business model innovation, entrepreneurship Venture capital, startup financing, and investment decision-making Responsible business, corporate governance, and AI governance Industry-linked projects, studios, and executive education and experience working across sectors such as financial services, healthcare, manufacturing, retail, logistics, consulting, technology, venture capital, or the public sector would be an asset. Key Responsibilities Develop and teach business-related courses and electives. Contribute to interdisciplinary teaching at the intersection of business, AI, technology, design, and society. Develop applied learning opportunities, for example, through projects, industry collaborations, internships, studios, case studies, and practitioner engagement. Build partnerships with industry, startups, public-sector, and innovation ecosystem partners. Mentor students and contribute to curriculum development, programme development and university service. Support executive education and lifelong learning initiatives where relevant. Contribute to SUTD’s broader industry engagement and thought leadership in business and AI. Qualifications Applicants should normally possess: Substantial industry, entrepreneurial, consulting, public-sector, or professional experience. Evidence of teaching ability or strong potential to translate professional expertise into engaging student learning. Active connections to relevant professional, industry, investment, entrepreneurial or innovation networks. Strong communication, collaborative, and stakeholder-engagement skills. Experience leading AI-enabled business transformation, organizational innovation, digital strategy, technology commercialization, entrepreneurship, venture investment/building, executive leadership, or consulting will be advantageous. Application Materials Applicants should submit: Curriculum Vitae and cover letter. A statement of professional experience, teaching and/or research interests, and fit with SUTD's Supercharged DAI and HASS priorities (maximum 2 pages). A brief proposal for one business elective or applied-learning initiative that could be developed at SUTD (maximum 2 pages). Two examples of teaching materials, teaching evaluations, executive education materials, or other evidence of teaching effectiveness, if available. Two examples of applied outputs or professional impact, such as publications, cases, consulting projects, venture initiatives, policy contributions, public writing, or industry projects. Contact details for three relevant referees from academia and/or industry. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Flexible arrangements, including secondments, fractional appointments, or visiting practitioner appointments, may be considered for outstanding candidates. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Member-Assistant-Professor-of-Practice-Lecturer-in-Design-%28HASS%29-138682/57935344/": {
      "title": "Faculty Member - Assistant Professor of Practice/ Lecturer in Design (HASS)",
      "description": "Faculty Member - Assistant Professor of Practice/ Lecturer in Design (HASS) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Member - Assistant Professor of Practice/ Lecturer in Design (HASS) Job Req ID: 2538 Employee Category: Faculty Department: HASS Job Description The Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences (HASS) cluster at the Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Practice in Design or Lecturer in Design. We are seeking an accomplished design researcher or design practitioner with an interest in driving pedagogical innovation at the interface of design thinking, technology, human-centred design, and artificial intelligence. The successful candidate should be able to help students use AI critically and creatively throughout the design process, while maintaining a strong grounding in human needs, material practice, prototyping, and real-world implementation. The candidate should have: Significant professional experience in design practice Evidence of success in the realization of design (products, services, systems, etc.) including experience with design manufacturing and links with industry An informed understanding of the opportunities, limitations, and responsible use of AI in design practice Evidence of excellence in teaching, mentoring, or facilitating studio-based and project-based learning Experience or capability for programme management and leadership is also a plus The successful candidate would play a critical role in new undergraduate and postgraduate offerings at SUTD that are central to SUTD's Design.AI vision, including: At the undergraduate level, developing and running Studio courses within the Design and Artificial Intelligence (DAI) programme At the postgraduate level, developing and running Design and Studio courses within the M.Eng. Innovation by Design programme and the MTD (Human-Centred Design) programme Guiding the introduction of Design.AI activities and pedagogy throughout the HASS and DAI curriculum Preferably able to integrate AI-enabled design methods, tools, and critical perspectives into studio teaching and project-based learning, and guide students in using AI to support problem framing, research, ideation, prototyping, testing, and implementation, while ensuring appropriate human judgement and oversight Application Details Candidates should submit the following materials: A cover letter A curriculum vitae A statement of teaching experience A statement of design research or design practice A portfolio documenting design practice Sample syllabi or proposals for two courses you may wish to offer Names, affiliations, and email addresses of three referees. (Please note that candidates who advance to the interview stage will be asked to submit two letters of recommendation. Please have your recommenders ready to send their letters via email or Interfolio.) About SUTD and HASS SUTD is a young and distinctive university with a mission to nurture technically grounded leaders and innovators. Today, SUTD's Design.AI vision means that artificial intelligence is not merely a tool but a partner in the design process; together, design and AI form the backbone of our curriculum and research. The university champions cohort-based learning and interdisciplinary pedagogy, offering degrees in Architecture and Sustainable Design (ASD), Design and Artificial Intelligence (DAI), Engineering Product Development (EPD), Engineering Systems and Design (ESD), and Information Systems Technology and Design (ISTD). The Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (HASS) Cluster plays a pivotal and critical role in the university’s commitment to world-class teaching and research excellence by providing the human-centred vision to achieve a better world by design. For more information, please visit the following websites: https://www.sutd.edu.sg/ https://hass.sutd.edu.sg/ https://www.sutd.edu.sg/dai/ https://www.sutd.edu.sg/programme-listing/mibd/about/programme-overview/ https://www.sutd.edu.sg/programme-listing/mtd-human-centred-design/ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.sutd.edu.sg/job/Singapore-Faculty-Position-Educator-Track-%28Engineering-Systems-and-Design%29-138682/13958744/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position",
      "description": "Faculty Position - Educator-Track (Engineering Systems and Design) Job Details | SUTD Skip to main content Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs Search by Keyword Clear Home Page Corporate Site Jobs by Category Faculty Jobs Researchers Jobs Admin Jobs View profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Department All Employee Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Position - Educator-Track (Engineering Systems and Design) Job Req ID: 998 Employee Category: Faculty Department: ESD Pillar The Engineering Systems and Design (ESD) pillar within the Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) is pursuing multiple, exceptional educator-track faculty hires at all levels (lecturer, senior lecturer, and principal lecturer). About SUTD and ESD The Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD) has topped the list of emerging engineering schools (MIT report, 2018) and possesses a unique structure and mission within the vibrant nation of Singapore. SUTD features the integration of design with engineering, an intimate student to faculty ratio, an innovative active learning pedagogy, an interdisciplinary pillar organization, a stellar faculty, and a beautiful new campus. The Engineering Systems and Design (ESD) pillar within SUTD offers exceptional undergraduate and doctoral degrees with focus on Business Analytics and Operations Research, Financial Services, Supply Chain and Logistics, and Aviation Systems. ESD undergraduates are prepared for a wide range of engineering and management careers in private and public sectors, including healthcare, banking, manufacturing, supply-chain, energy, transportation, and entertainment and hospitality. They are equally adept at entrepreneurship and boldly initiating start-up ventures. Job Requirements for Educator-Track Faculty We seek to fill positions in several areas including but not restricted to statistical and machine learning (ML), artificial intelligence (AI), operations research, data science, and industrial engineering, with applications to aviation, healthcare, sustainability, supply chains and logistics, urban mobility, and quantitative finance. The successful candidates should be specialised in an engineering systems-related field and have solid grounding in one or more systems methodologies including, but not limited to, AI/ML, optimization, stochastic modelling, statistics, game theory, financial engineering, and simulation. Empirical, experimental, computational, and analytical research approaches are all welcome. Candidates must be committed to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching-Track faculty can develop and maintain an active research program per their interest. Successful candidates can look forward to competitive remuneration, assistance for relocation to Singapore and attractive research grant opportunities. A candidate’s full application package should include: 1.    A cover letter 2.    Curriculum Vitae (CV), including publications 3.    Teaching statement / plans 4.    Research statement / plans, if any 5.    Contact information of 3 referees How to apply Applications are being accepted online and the review of applications is ongoing. Additional information about the university and the Engineering Systems and Design pillar can be found at https://sutd.esd.edu.sg/ . For direct enquiries contact Associate Professor Carlos Gerardo Murguia Rendon, murguia_rendon@sutd.edu.sg . Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Jobs About Student Development Campus Life Admissions Education Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2022 Singapore University of Technology and Design (SUTD). All Rights Reserved."
    }
